Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032506/state.json" "file_sha256" "0e9943478b35891f7ec97098737cb707e521dc2c7b6bebffb4d2f4b02bd7dc95" "basis" 1224 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032506/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-130313" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 6 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032506/state.json" "file_sha256" "0e9943478b35891f7ec97098737cb707e521dc2c7b6bebffb4d2f4b02bd7dc95" "basis" 1224 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032506/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-130313" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}7 & -7 & -21 \\\\ 3 & -3 & -9 \\\\ -8 & 8 & 24\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032506/state.json" "file_sha256" "0e9943478b35891f7ec97098737cb707e521dc2c7b6bebffb4d2f4b02bd7dc95" "basis" 1224 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032506/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-319938" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $ABC$, where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $ABC=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  |\n|  |  | {{field-3}} |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032506/state.json" "file_sha256" "0e9943478b35891f7ec97098737cb707e521dc2c7b6bebffb4d2f4b02bd7dc95" "basis" 1224 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032506/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-319938" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, recall the associative law\n\n$$\nABC=(AB)C=A(BC).\n$$\n\nNotice that $A$ is a $3\\times 1$ matrix, $B$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix, and $C$ is a $2\\times 1$ matrix. Therefore, \n\n- multiplying $A$ by $B$, we will obtain a $3\\times 2$ matrix, which will require finding $6$ entries, while\n\n- multiplying $B$ by $C$, we will obtain a $1\\times 1$ matrix, which will require finding only $1$ entry.\n\nSo, we find the product $BC$ first: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-13\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply $A$ by $BC:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ABC & =A(BC) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-13\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-65 \\\\ 13 \\\\ -39\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032506/state.json" "file_sha256" "0e9943478b35891f7ec97098737cb707e521dc2c7b6bebffb4d2f4b02bd7dc95" "basis" 1224 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032506/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-319938" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032506/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "89049547bc2ffed2ec35f0c0204dfa13ffa0ed66549f6a44d4756c843dc4eabb" "basis" 1224 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032506/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-319938" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_wi